Subject: Leave safe allocations unlocked under Fil-C
Origin: Filnix
Upstream-Status: Not submitted

cryptsetup 2.8 mlock()s every crypt_safe_alloc heap object and treats
failure as non-fatal (as when over RLIMIT_MEMLOCK). The Fil-C runtime only
permits mlock on mmapped memory and traps on malloc'd objects, which aborted
luksFormat and the bitlk/fvault2/unit-utils-crypt tests. Take the existing
unlocked path instead; crypt_safe_free already skips munlock for it.

--- a/lib/utils_safe_memory.c
+++ b/lib/utils_safe_memory.c
@@ -54,8 +54,11 @@ void *crypt_safe_alloc(size_t size)
 	alloc->size = size;
 
 	/* Ignore failure if it is over limit. */
+#ifndef __FILC__
+	/* Fil-C only locks mmapped memory and traps on heap objects. */
 	if (!mlock(alloc, size + OVERHEAD))
 		alloc->locked = true;
+#endif
 
 	/* coverity[leaked_storage] */
 	return &alloc->data;
